WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.113 --> 00:00:02.000
The prime numbers look like randomness.

2
00:00:02.275 --> 00:00:07.312
But their distribution follows a hidden orchestra: the zeros of the Riemann zeta function.

3
00:00:07.575 --> 00:00:11.375
The Riemann Hypothesis says: all of them lie on one single line.

4
00:00:11.425 --> 00:00:15.450
Unproven — for more than one hundred and sixty-five years.

5
00:00:16.985 --> 00:00:20.460
The TFPT builds the E8 lattice from two axioms.

6
00:00:20.722 --> 00:00:26.284
Its counting function already knows the primes: each one acts as its own Hecke check channel.

7
00:00:26.547 --> 00:00:29.635
And the zeta function appears as a shadow of this geometry.

8
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:33.308
From this bookkeeping came a window matrix.

9
00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:38.183
And it turned out to be something classical: word for word, Suzuki's localized Weil operator.

10
00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:44.682
That is the W1 theorem — machine-verified, with one honestly documented erratum.

11
00:00:46.121 --> 00:00:48.146
The same window form is a detector.

12
00:00:48.408 --> 00:00:54.670
Calibrated on solved worlds: Ramanujan graphs — where the analogue is proven — pass the test.

13
00:00:54.933 --> 00:01:01.120
Epstein zeta functions — with genuine zeros off the line — break it, exactly as predicted.

14
00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:06.946
And the matched filter makes this constructive: any off-line zero would produce a computable witness.

15
00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.933
The object is falsifiable.

16
00:01:10.468 --> 00:01:12.693
Two theorems stand on the whole surface.

17
00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:22.305
The sign of the determinant: unconditionally proven, on all sixty-seven windows — the century-old zero-free region blocks the only escape route.

18
00:01:22.568 --> 00:01:27.655
And the margin: sixty of seventy windows, closed with cited classical results.

19
00:01:28.612 --> 00:01:39.162
Then, August third: in the graph laboratory, where the analogue is proven, the target decomposition exists exactly — a sum of squares plus a defect.

20
00:01:39.212 --> 00:01:41.550
Our window form is built identically.

21
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.912
One part is missing: the engine, Z1.

22
00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:47.262
Hilbert–Pólya, in window coordinates.

23
00:01:47.956 --> 00:01:55.243
And the geometry supplies the measure: the prime atoms can be read off, without circularity, from lattice counting alone.

24
00:01:55.518 --> 00:01:59.518
The gamma flow forces their masses to per mille — and their positions.

25
00:01:59.806 --> 00:02:03.143
But honestly: as a test bench, not as a generator.

26
00:02:04.145 --> 00:02:08.945
The state today: every mass lives in a corridor with exactly computable edges.

27
00:02:09.207 --> 00:02:15.257
The arithmetic does not choose the edge — it chooses an interior point, at zero point five three.

28
00:02:15.507 --> 00:02:18.357
An energy extremum hits it to within per mille.

29
00:02:18.632 --> 00:02:22.307
The open question: explain the selection inside the corridor.

30
00:02:23.716 --> 00:02:25.004
No proof of RH.

31
00:02:25.279 --> 00:02:28.053
This program says so itself, at every step.

32
00:02:28.329 --> 00:02:32.204
But the question has never been this small — and never this precise.

33
00:02:32.466 --> 00:02:35.729
Almost nine hundred modules, every number machine-checked.

34
00:02:36.003 --> 00:02:37.204
This is the Prime Front.

35
00:02:39.233 --> 00:02:53.270
Since then, the sigma chain has turned the finite question into a regional theorem: every matrix whose entry data lie in the certified region is positive definite — a proof object, checkable by a tiny program anyone can run.

36
00:02:53.545 --> 00:02:59.508
One construction problem remains: a predefined window sequence, cofinal, staying inside the region.

37
00:02:59.558 --> 00:03:04.120
The proof object is ready for audit — the RH quantifier is not.
